.Dd @MDOCDATE@
.Dt CLOWNFILE 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm clownfile
.Nd clown per-instance configuration file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A
.Nm
is a TOML file that sets per-directory defaults for a clown session (RFC-0013).
clown discovers clownfiles by ascending from the current directory to
.Ev HOME ,
merging them so a
.Nm
closer to the current directory overrides one closer to
.Ev HOME ,
per key.
An absent
.Nm
is not an error; a malformed one is.
.Pp
This page documents the
.Sy [profile]
table; the
.Sy [attach]
table (multiplexer templates) is reserved for a future release.
.Ss [profile]
The
.Sy [profile]
table provides defaults layered beneath explicit command-line flags and
environment variables.
The named-profile registry
.Pq Fl -profile
is a separate mechanism and wins over these defaults.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy provider
The provider (claude, codex, circus, opencode, crush).
Applied only when neither
.Fl -provider
nor
.Ev CLOWN_PROVIDER
is set; a clownfile provider also suppresses the interactive profile picker.
.It Sy backend
The tent container backend (podman or lima) used by
.Fl -tent .
.It Sy model
The model.
Injected as
.Fl -model
for the claude-family providers (claude, circus, clownbox) when the user has not
already passed
.Fl -model ;
other providers source their model elsewhere.
.It Sy [profile.env]
A table of environment variables exported into the provider and its plugin
servers, set only when not already present (the ambient environment wins).
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[profile]
provider = "claude"
model = "claude-sonnet-4-6"

[profile.env]
ANTHROPIC_LOG = "info"
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clown-chat 1 ,
.Xr clown-job 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC-0013 (clownfile, per-instance identity, and clown-owned chat).
